# HAR Harness Workflow

This repository uses `.har/` agent harnesses. Follow this workflow on every change.

The harness is **how you run the project**, not only how you verify it. To see an app
live (manual testing, browser sessions, screenshots), launch a slot — never hand-roll
docker/dev-server startup; the harness already encodes DB setup, ports, and env.
If a harness command fails, fix the harness or surface the failure — do not quietly
work around it with ad-hoc commands.

## Harnesses in this repo

Monorepo with two harnesses — pick by the files you are changing:

| Path | Runs | Use when changing |
|------|------|-------------------|
| `.har/` | `@har/cli` (typecheck, unit tests, build) | `src/`, `packages/`, `tests/` |
| `control/.har/` | Mission Control (Next.js + Postgres, browser-e2e) | `control/` |

Run harness commands from the directory that owns the harness (e.g. `cd control && ./.har/launch.sh 1`).

## Before making changes

1. Read [AGENT.md](./AGENT.md) at the repo root (harness index) — for webapp work also [control/AGENT.md](./control/AGENT.md)
2. Read the owning harness's `README.md` and `stages.json` (e.g. [.har/README.md](./.har/README.md), [.har/stages.json](./.har/stages.json))
3. After launch, read the harness's `CLAUDE.agent.md` for slot URLs and definition of done

## After making changes

Validate through the harness — do not skip verification or substitute ad-hoc npm/test commands.

### 1. HAR MCP (preferred — configured in `.cursor/mcp.json`)

- `har_launch_environment` with `agentId: 1` — once per session if not already launched
- `har_run_verification` with `agentId: 1` — fast loop (typecheck + unit tests)
- `har_run_verification` with `agentId: 1, full: true` — required before declaring work done (+ lint + build)
- `har_teardown_environment` with `agentId: 1` — cleanup when finished

### 2. HAR CLI (when `har` is installed)

```bash
har env launch 1
har env verify 1
har env verify 1 --full
har env teardown 1
```

### 3. Shell fallback (no CLI/MCP installed)

```bash
./.har/launch.sh 1
./.har/verify.sh 1
./.har/verify.sh 1 --full
./.har/teardown.sh 1
```

Work happens in an isolated git worktree by default (`~/worktrees/har_project-agent-<id>`). If your IDE workspace is the worktree, pass `--repo /path/to/main/checkout` to CLI commands; MCP is already configured with the main checkout path.

## Definition of done

- Full verification returns pass (`har env verify 1 --full`, MCP `har_run_verification` with `full: true`, or `./.har/verify.sh 1 --full`)
- New behavior has automated test coverage (typecheck, tests, lint, build)
- Do not declare work complete without running full verify
